GodotSim 🎮📊
A real-time, animated Discrete Event Simulator built inside the Godot Game Engine.

GodotSim integrates SimSharp (a .NET discrete-event simulation library) with Godot 4 (C# / Mono) to produce an open-source simulation tool that combines rigorous simulation logic with real-time visual feedback — something most commercial DES platforms (Arena, SIMUL8, AnyLogic) do not offer at zero cost.

🎓 Developed as an MSc Business Analytics dissertation project at the University of Surrey (Sept 2025).
Supervisor: Dr. Wolfgang Garn


🖥️ Demo
UI Controls
Agent Animation
CSV Output
Configure agents, trials, speed
Animated agents flow: Spawn → Queue → Server → Exit
Per-trial metrics saved automatically



🔍 What It Does
GodotSim simulates an M/M/1 queue (single-server queueing system) and animates the results in real time inside a Godot scene. Key capabilities:

Configurable parameters — arrival rate (λ), service rate (μ), number of agents, trial runs, animation speed
Batch trial support — run N simulations back-to-back; aggregated statistics across all trials
Real-time animation — agents spawn, queue, get served, and exit with smooth movement driven by actual simulation timestamps
Automatic CSV logging — two output files generated per session:
output_events.csv — per-agent timestamps (Arrival, QueueEnter, ServiceStart, Leave)
output_summary.csv — per-trial KPIs (λ, μ, ρ, Avg Wait, Avg System Time, Utilisation, Runtime)
Performance benchmarked against SimPy (Python) — GodotSim is competitive and faster than text-only tools, with modest overhead from animation rendering


🏗️ Architecture
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐

│                   Godot Engine                  │

│                                                 │

│  ┌──────────────┐     ┌───────────────────────┐ │

│  │ SimulationUi │────▶│   SimSharpEngine.cs   │ │

│  │     .cs      │     │  (DES Logic / M/M/1)  │ │

│  └──────────────┘     └──────────┬────────────┘ │

│         │                        │               │

│         │              EventLog (List<AgentEvent>)

│         │                        │               │

│         ▼                        ▼               │

│  ┌──────────────┐     ┌───────────────────────┐ │

│  │  CSVLogger   │     │  AnimationManager.cs  │ │

│  │  (output)    │     │  (Visual Playback)    │ │

│  └──────────────┘     └───────────────────────┘ │

└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

         ▲

         │ Embedded source (not DLL)

┌────────────────────┐

│   SimSharp/        │

│  (simulation core) │

└────────────────────┘
Key Design Decision
SimSharp's source files are embedded directly into the Godot project rather than referenced as an external DLL. This avoids .NET assembly compatibility issues between SimSharp's build targets and Godot Mono, and keeps the project fully self-contained.


📁 Project Structure
godotsim/

├── scripts/

│   ├── SimSharpEngine.cs     # Core DES logic — M/M/1 queue, monitors, event log

│   ├── AnimationManager.cs   # Godot Node2D — animates agents from EventLog

│   ├── SimulationUi.cs       # UI controller — wires inputs to engine and logger

│   ├── CSVLogger.cs          # Writes output_events.csv and output_summary.csv

│   └── AgentEvent.cs         # Data class — per-agent timestamps

├── SimSharp/                 # SimSharp source (embedded, not DLL)

│   ├── Core/                 # Simulation environment, events, resources

│   ├── Analysis/             # SampleMonitor, TimeSeriesMonitor

│   ├── Collections/          # Priority queue internals

│   └── Random/               # PCG random distributions

├── scenes/

│   ├── Main.tscn             # Root scene (UI entry point)

│   ├── sim_scene.tscn        # Animation scene (spawns agents)

│   └── agent.tscn            # Individual agent node

├── GodotSim.csproj

├── GodotSim.sln

└── icon.svg


